  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Defense obligated $286B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense made 2,388,908 awards with an average award size of $120K. Obligations are down 41.9% year over year, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Fiscal-year obligations were $387B in FY21, $414B in FY22, $457B in FY23, $446B in FY24, and $492B in FY25, before the FY26 to date total of $286B. The largest spending categories in FY2026 to date include Aircraft Manufacturing at $35.4B, Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $26.2B, and Engineering Services at $25.6B. The top vendors in FY2026 to date include LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $10.6B and $10.4B, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION at $8.6B, and RAYTHEON COMPANY at $8.1B.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the scale and recent trend in Defense contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $286B in FY2026 to date. Obligations are down 41.9% year over year. The Department of Defense made 2,388,908 awards at an average award size of $120K. Fiscal-year totals show obligations of $387B in FY21, $414B in FY22, $457B in FY23, $446B in FY24, and $492B in FY25."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and companies capture most Defense dollars?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest industry in FY2026 to date at $35.4B, followed by Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $26.2B and Engineering Services at $25.6B. The Department of Defense’s top vendors in FY2026 to date include LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $10.6B and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $10.4B, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION at $8.6B, and RAYTHEON COMPANY at $8.1B. Other major vendors are THE BOEING COMPANY at $5.9B and HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC at $5.5B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Defense spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense obligated $286B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense’s fiscal-year obligations were $387B in FY21, $414B in FY22, $457B in FY23, $446B in FY24, and $492B in FY25, and the FY26 total is partial. The Department of Defense made 2,388,908 awards at an average award size of $120K."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Defense buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense buys aerospace, weapons systems, engineering, R&D, construction, and health services. Top industry categories in FY2026 to date include Aircraft Manufacturing at $35.4B, Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $26.2B, Engineering Services at $25.6B, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $20.4B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Defense's largest contractors?",
      "a": "LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION is the top-named vendor entries in FY2026 to date at $10.6B and $10.4B. Other top vendors in FY2026 to date include ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION at $8.6B, RAYTHEON COMPANY at $8.1B, THE BOEING COMPANY at $5.9B and $5.1B, HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC at $5.5B, AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP at $4.8B, TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP at $4.7B, and RTX CORPORATION at $3.8B."
